# Phase 9 - Trivy vulnerability exceptions (NARROW, JUSTIFIED, TIME-BOUNDED).
#
# Policy (see docs/provenance/phase9_devsecops.md, "Gate 6"):
#   * The container gate fails on any FIXABLE HIGH/CRITICAL (--ignore-unfixed).
#   * Unfixed OS/base-image CVEs are reported but not blocking (no upstream fix
#     exists; remediation belongs to the base image, addressed in Phase 10 by
#     moving to a hardened/distroless base).
#   * This file lists ONLY specific advisories reviewed and judged
#     non-exploitable in THIS runtime. It is not a blanket ignore: any NEW
#     fixable HIGH/CRITICAL (in app deps or OS packages) still fails CI.
#
# Each entry below is a copy of a build-tool dependency that pip/setuptools
# VENDOR internally (pip/_vendor/*, setuptools/_vendor/*). They are used only by
# the package installer, are never imported by `uvicorn backend.app:app`, and
# pip is never invoked inside the immutable, non-root, read-only runtime
# container. The importable setuptools in the image is already 79.0.1 (patched);
# Trivy flags a stale vendored dist-info. Reviewed 2026-09-28.
# FOLLOW-UP (Phase 10): adopt a slim/distroless base that ships no pip/setuptools
# in the runtime layer, then delete these entries and re-scan.

# setuptools PackageIndex path traversal - triggered only when installing from
# an index at runtime; never happens in this image. Importable setuptools=79.0.1.
CVE-2025-47273

# wheel privilege escalation via malicious wheel - only during `pip install` of
# an untrusted wheel; the runtime container never installs packages.
CVE-2026-24049

# jaraco.context path traversal via malicious tar - vendored by setuptools; only
# reachable through setuptools' install-time archive handling.
CVE-2026-23949

# msgpack OOB read on Unpacker reuse - vendored by pip; the application request
# path uses JSON/pydantic, never msgpack, and pip is not run at runtime.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# urllib3 (two HIGH) vendored by pip at pip/_vendor/urllib3 == 2.7.0. Confirmed by
# inspecting the built image: the IMPORTABLE urllib3 is pinned to 2.8.0 (patched;
# docker/requirements-runtime.txt), 0 findings. The only flagged copy is the one
# pip bundles for its OWN installer HTTP client. Both CVEs require urllib3 to make
# HTTP requests, which happens only during `pip install`; pip is NEVER invoked in
# the immutable, non-root, read-only runtime container (CMD is uvicorn only). Same
# class as the pip/setuptools-vendored entries above. Reviewed 2026-10-10.
# FOLLOW-UP (Phase 10): the planned slim/distroless base that ships no pip in the
# runtime layer removes this vendored copy entirely; delete these two then.
# CVE-2026-97687: urllib3 traffic interception via HTTPS proxy TLS (fixed 2.8.0).
CVE-2026-97687
# CVE-2026-97689: urllib3 DoS via unbounded memory (fixed 2.8.0).
CVE-2026-97689
